CAIOS deploys these components rather than forking them. Where a value that
should have been configuration was hardcoded upstream, the change is carried as
a patch rather than as a modified copy.

MODIFICATIONS
-------------

Apache License 2.0 section 4(b) requires that modified files carry prominent
notices stating that they were changed. Every modification CAIOS makes to
Apache-2.0 licensed source is held in `patches/`, one patch per change, each
pinned to the upstream commit it was written against. `patches/README.md`
records what each patch changes and why the value could not be configuration.
That directory and that file together are this project's statement of changes.

The patches are applied at container build time to a copy under `build/`.
`vendor/` holds unmodified upstream source and is never edited.

THIRD-PARTY CONTENT NOT COVERED BY THIS NOTICE
----------------------------------------------

The marketplace catalogue lists containerised models that are neither authored
nor licensed by this project. Each carries its own licence, stated in its own
repository — several are not Apache-2.0. Notably `ai4os-yolo-torch` wraps
Ultralytics YOLO, which is AGPL-3.0.

Models offered through the AI4Life loader come from bioimage.io and carry
per-model licences. Language models offered through the LLM tool come from
Hugging Face and carry their own licences and acceptable-use terms.

Deploying a model through CAIOS does not relicense it.
